/**
@page applications_exahype2_airglow Airglow chemistry

This example couples 3D gravity‐wave dynamics with a simplified airglow chemistry
model in the mesosphere and lower thermosphere. Background temperature and composition
profiles are imported from external atmosphere models (e.g. NRLMSISE), and are then used to
construct steady states for the major species \f$ (\text{O}, \text{O}_2, \text{N}_2, \text{O}_3) \f$ and the airglow emitters
(OH vibrational levels, excited oxygen).

On top of this steady background, ExaHyPE 2 evolves a finite–volume Godunov solver that transports the chemical species with
prescribed winds and applies height-dependent production and loss terms.
Different sets of Einstein coefficients can be selected to study how the gravity waves
modulate the airglow layer and its emission bands.

*/
